gnozzard (0.1.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add optional per-workplace automatic window arrangement, off by default.
  * Own and reversibly disable native and conflicting extension tiling.
  * Use four-pixel tile gaps and outer margins with shared-edge handles.
  * Reconcile application geometry changes and fit new windows beside groups.
  * Accept real screen-edge and corner drops and explain minimum-size limits.
  * Add independent top-bar and taskbar auto-hide settings using native struts.
  * Widen both immediate bar activation strips to four pixels.
  * Remove taskbars while tiling; reuse Applications in the system bar.
  * Add taskbar visibility modes, swap bar positions and simplify settings.
  * Share GNOME's native panel-menu manager without nested Applications grabs.
  * Align Applications using the same label layout as the workplace buttons.
  * Keep Applications attached to its bar and hold that bar while open.
  * Disconnect menu callbacks before destroying a removed taskbar controller.
  * Share workplace moves and Force Kill with GNOME's native titlebar menu.
  * Disable taskbar-only controls when no taskbar exists; shorten mode labels.
  * Avoid GNOME 46 unmaximize loops and improve client-size handling.
  * Refit invalid splits with client sizes; preserve older windows on overflow.
  * Associate asynchronous resize replies with outstanding configure requests.
  * Keep pending requests through workplace changes and earlier client frames.
  * Add optional edge switching between existing workplaces, off by default.
  * Clarify the bar-swapping label in both settings interfaces.
  * Older-GNOME tiling resize transitions still need broader validation.

 -- Open Research Tools <openresearchtools@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 02:05:46 +0100

